Z||000003||Fleabitdog||05-13-2001||10:46 AM||||Woof!!! Yea I had to go hit ahydrant, could not find one so I had to make do on a Trans ams tire.It was a great show, some very nice cars. Congratulations on 1st place Vernonica V6 GT. You did a very nice job skinning those seats. And Congrats on your trophy 84bill. Thanks for taking all the pics. I think my fav car there was Chads killer kreation GT. The engine looked very good rockcrawl. Nice clean job.Can't wait to see skitimes finished TTop. Looking forward to Carlisle. BTW anybody interested in a 3800? There is one in the yard at Carlisle <BR>( missing supercharger) for 400.00 Also a 3800 in an olds with 55,000(not supercharged for 450.00. Thanks Dave||||reg||1
Z||000004||84Bill||05-13-2001||12:14 PM||||The stream Video's are up. <P>Hey glad to see you made it back Fleabit! Nice to see those Trans Am wheels get put to good use   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"><P>Nice job on that engine Rock, I'll be looking for you and Chad at Carlisle.<P>Congrats again Veronica and Ski on your Trophy and Happy Mothers day!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  2 for 2!<P>I was giggling all night about my trophy  LOL.<P>Thanks to all you other Fiero owners for not showing up at Englishtown. You made it possible for me to win and next year will be another shurefire win.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif"> hehehehe.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by 84Bill (edited 05-13-2001).]||||reg||14
